y but no evidence points toward a Democratic shift.", "watch": "Any credible statewide polling or a major national swing toward the Democratic nominee could move this from Lean R toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Indiana remains a Republican-leaning state in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly nine points toward the GOP. The 2026 primary season reinforced that picture, with coverage describing continued Trump-aligned dominance in Indiana Republican politics and no signs of a competitive statewide Democratic operation at the presidential level. No incumbent president is on the ballot, which removes one familiar advantage but does not alter the state's underlying lean.\n\nNo public polls, expert ratings, or prediction-market pricing are available for this race, so the forecast relies on fundamentals. That thin evidence base widens the uncertainty, but nothing in recent headlines suggests Indiana is trending toward the Democrats. The race is rated Lean Republican, with the GOP favored but not to the point of certainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1505, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2049, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2014, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2053, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2035, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1986, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2114, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2139, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2074, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2042, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2034, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2041, "marg